  "worker_judgment_notes": "Multi-layer contract (first use of the schema's 'sources' array): Aurora PD publishes 2024 incidents as 8 separate per-offense ArcGIS FeatureServers under the org (0Va1ID99NSrNyyPX, owner A_ESRI_KHughes) backing its own transparency hub apd-transparency-portal-auroraco.hub.arcgis.com -- APD_RMS_{Burglary,Robbery,Homicide,Aggravated_Assault,Motor_Vehicle_Theft,Sexual_Assault,Arson}_Public plus APD_RMS_Theft_View (note the _View naming for theft only), all at sublayer id 36 (not 0). Identity was independently re-verified 2026-07-08 before onboarding (Agency field = 100% 'Aurora PD' on every layer, real Aurora CO neighborhood names, org/domain ownership chain; the Aurora IL lookalike hub is a confirmed-different org). City field is null on all layers -- identity rests on Agency + org + neighborhoods. Native geometry is EPSG:2232 Colorado Central state plane (feet); the runner's standard outSR=4326 request reprojects server-side, verified in-range for Aurora CO (39.5-39.9N, -104.9 to -104.4W). ARSON LAYER EXCLUDED: arson (89 rows 2024) is not one of the seven canonical offenses; the layer is intentionally not in this contract. Full-data per-layer NIBRS purity verification (all 16,191 in-scope 2024 rows pulled, not sampled): homicide layer = 100% 09A (35/35, no 09B negligent manslaughter / 09C justifiable homicide present at all); robbery = 100% 120; aggravated_assault = 100% 13A (no 13B/13C contamination); burglary = 100% 220; motor_vehicle_theft = 100% 240; sexual_assault = exactly 11A (191) + 11B (51) + 11C (42), which is precisely the FBI revised (2013+) rape definition with no 11D fondling and no 36-series non-forcible codes -- maps directly to our 'rape' with zero exclusions needed; theft = 8,167 rows of 23A-23H larceny codes PLUS 8 stray rows of 26A (Fraud Offenses), the only layer broader than its name -- the 23-series in-list rule excludes the 26A rows by construction (larceny mapped count 8,167 pre-bounds). Offense rules are layer-scoped (each rule conditions on __source_slug AND NIBRSCode) so a stray code in the wrong layer can never cross-contaminate an offense. id_fields = [__source_slug, OBJECTID]: OBJECTID is unique within each layer (verified 0 duplicates per layer), and slug-prefixing keeps a multi-offense incident that legitimately appears in two layers (same OffenseId/CallId) counted once per offense, matching per-offense NIBRS semantics. ReportYear=2024 server-side filter and the runner's ReportDate-derived year filter agree exactly (0 year-filter drops on all 7 layers); ReportDate is epoch-ms and is handled by the runner's epoch-ms fallback. Bounds are the raw TIGER/crosswalk-touching Aurora block-group envelope (273 BGs raw-touching jurisdiction 08:municipal:place:0804000; minx/miny/maxx/maxy -104.886613,39.518327,-104.413963,39.956417) padded 0.02 deg; 12 of 16,191 rows (8 theft, 3 MVT, 1 sexual assault) fall outside and are dropped. Aurora spans Arapahoe/Adams/Douglas counties; the BG universe comes from the jurisdiction crosswalk, so county lines are irrelevant. Coordinate coverage is 100% on every layer (0 null geometries). Reconciliation against state/controls/jurisdiction_controls_2024.parquet (all cius_publication_annual, quality tier high): robbery 545/542=1.006, motor_vehicle_theft 3618/3567=1.014, rape 283/292=0.969, burglary 1364/1477=0.924 all inside the strict 10% gate (feed_total_candidate); murder 35/41=0.854, larceny 8159/7305=1.117, aggravated_assault 2167/2896=0.748 outside it (share_only) -- the aggravated-assault gap plausibly reflects the feed being offense-record-level vs the control's victim-count basis and/or partial-year record suppression on the public layer, and murder's gap (6 events) is small-n; neither is treated as a source-identity problem given four offenses reconcile tightly. Rape maps cleanly here but the repo's rape default-deny texture policy applies regardless of this feed's quality. Contract is share-lane only per the standard generic-runner convention; the strict 10% gate decides feed-total-candidate status per offense, not admission of the contract.",
